WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.440
In the last years of Later Tang, the great general Shi Jingtang, who held a large army, decided to rise up and overthrow Later Tang's rule.

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:11.030
He gazed north, his eyes resolute.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:19.252
To improve his chances, Shi Jingtang sent a messenger north to ask the powerful Khitan for help.

00:00:19.602 --> 00:00:22.458
The messenger rode swiftly north on a fast horse.

00:00:22.808 --> 00:00:28.448
The Khitan chief agreed at once to send troops, dispatching a great force of elite cavalry southward.

00:00:28.798 --> 00:00:34.582
With the help of the Khitan cavalry, Shi Jingtang defeated the Later Tang armies again and again.

00:00:34.932 --> 00:00:42.204
In the year 936, Shi Jingtang founded Later Jin at Taiyuan and became its founding emperor.

00:00:42.554 --> 00:00:51.746
After taking the throne, Shi Jingtang honoured the Khitan ruler as a father, and every year sent him great quantities of gold, silver and cloth.

00:00:52.096 --> 00:01:00.064
This borrowing of troops completely changed the situation in the north, and planted a far-reaching hidden danger for the later problem of the Yanyun Sixteen Prefectures.

00:01:00.414 --> 00:01:03.366
The setting sun shone on the mountains and rivers of the north.

